"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. Preoperative PSA was 3.9. The surgical findings included a Gleason 3+4 with tertiary pattern 5 (ISUP grade group 2), positive surgical margins, and the absence of seminal vesicle invasion and lymph node metastasis. The biopsy revealed a higher grade of Gleason 3+5 (ISUP grade group 4) with perineural invasion. The absence of lymph node metastasis is a favorable finding.\n\nCountervailing factors include the positive surgical margins and the higher grade identified on biopsy compared to the resection specimen. Missing postoperative PSA or follow-up data significantly widens the uncertainty regarding the trajectory of recurrence. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and subsequent changes would be crucial in refining this prognosis. The current heuristic sensitivity range suggests a potential recurrence horizon within a specific timeframe. The fixed estimated horizon is 31.81 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 25.45–38.17 months; its coverage has not been validated."
